25,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
26,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It seems some potential members are deterred by a full year's commitment upfront, and mid-year joins are a manual headache.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The treasurer's workload is skewed; chasing individual payments is a nightmare compared to a single annual collection.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The usage is incredibly uneven. A small group does all the work and attends everything, while some pay but never show up.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,Charging for specific events seems to have killed the habit of attending weekday meetings. People are overthinking the cost of coming.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Most of our costs are fixed—hall hire and insurance—regardless of attendance. Also, many members struggle to pay the full fee at once.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if the costs are fixed, we can't rely solely on per-event fees.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, if a few people do everything, a flat fee might feel like a subsidy for the inactive.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,Exactly. It's a point of contention among the regulars.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"But @Asuka, if we make it too rigid, we lose the casual atmosphere that makes the club work.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"We need a balance. We can't afford to lose money, but we can't make the treasurer quit.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, would a tiered system help the treasurer, or just add more categories to track?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Likely more categories. Simplicity is key for the person holding the books.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I think we need to acknowledge the difference in usage without making it a barrier.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm worried that any ""tier"" or ""grade"" will make people feel they don't belong if they aren't ""top tier.""","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Takumi,,I just want a figure we can actually count on.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
